# Vercel env vars for the Clow landing (clow_landing.html + api/*).
# Copy VALUES into: Vercel dashboard → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# Never commit filled values.
#
# The waitlist endpoint tries backends in this order and returns 200 on
# first success. Both are OPTIONAL — if neither is set, signups still
# return 200 (client-side Plausible + localStorage catch them).

# ── Backend 1: gtm-engine on Fly.io (recommended) ────────────────────
# Full ICP scoring, deal pipeline, hot-lead Slack alerts, KafCa events.
# Deploy gtm-engine first: `cd clow-agents/backend && fly deploy -c gtm-engine/fly.toml`
GTM_ENGINE_URL=https://gtm-engine.fly.dev
GTM_ENGINE_TOKEN=match-the-API_TOKEN-you-set-on-gtm-engine

# ── Backend 2: GitHub Issues (zero-vendor fallback) ──────────────────
# Each waitlist signup becomes one labeled issue in a repo you own.
# Free forever. Create a fine-grained PAT with `issues:write` scope on
# ONE repo (recommended: a private repo just for the waitlist).
#   github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
GH_TOKEN=github_pat_replace_me
GH_REPO=your-github/clow-waitlist
